# Promo video build products.
#
# The finished MP4 ships as a release asset, not in the tree: at ~22 MB it would
# be by far the heaviest thing here and every rebuild would add another copy to
# history forever. The frames and the intermediate core are regenerated by
# `npx tsx tools/capture-ui.ts` and `python tools/make-promo.py`, and they SHOULD
# be regenerated rather than kept — a stale screenshot of a price is the one
# thing this repository exists to prevent.
assets/promo-frames/
assets/core.mp4
assets/*-promo.mp4
assets/.bed-looped.mp3
.promo-fonts/

# The generative bookends, same reasoning — the hero alone is 28 MB.
#
# These are the one promo input that cannot be regenerated from the repository,
# and the 2026-08-04 re-cut paid $4.80 to learn it: they were ignored by no rule
# in particular, never committed, and simply gone. The fix is not to commit
# them. It is that docs/PROMO.md now carries the exact prompts, seeds and model
# settings, so an identical pair is one API call away.
assets/hero.mp4
assets/endcard.mp4

# The MCP server's bundle. Built by `npm run build` in mcp/ and published to
# npm from CI; committing it would put a generated 37 KB file in every diff.
mcp/dist/

# Claude Code's working directory. Git worktrees are created under
# .claude/worktrees/<branch>, so this is a complete second copy of the
# repository nested inside the first — never something to commit.
.claude/
